<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        APNs environment. `production` is correct for BOTH TestFlight and the App Store; `development` is
        only for a debug build signed with a development profile. Getting this wrong is silent: APNs accepts
        the registration and drops every message, because a token minted in one environment is not valid in
        the other.

        ⚠️ This file is deliberately NOT at Platforms/iOS/Entitlements.plist. The .NET iOS SDK auto-detects
        that exact path and, once it exists, REQUIRES code signing for every build - including the unsigned
        Release build the "Mobile - iOS Build" CI job performs, which has no certificate and no profile.
        Gating CodesignEntitlements on IosSigned does not help, because it is the file's presence at the
        conventional path that triggers it, not the property. Verified by bisecting a build failure:
        "No valid iOS code signing keys found in keychain."

        Referenced explicitly from the csproj, only when IosSigned=true.
    -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
